                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Don't let the cards and achievements fool you, this is not a remaster. The resolution options are terrible and you are forced to play in an ugly window just to see text. Yea they just slapped it out there.\nSo why a positive? Because its playable, it doesn't auto skip cutscenes like harvester, and it has some support. Cards and achievements, most of ND's visual novel stock excluding blade runner is bare bone slap it on the store cash ins. In the days of steam, cards, badges, profiles, and achievements. Having no support at all makes your game equal to an archive file. Having something more gives it some legitimacy other than, here ya go barebone art we never gave a crap about. Am not accusing ND of this, ND remasters plenty. Accusing the industry of this, but this one was given more attention.\n\nAs for the game itself, seems ok so far, pretty weird art and atmosphere. Visual novel point and click style but its done well with a lot of good effects.",
